**Temple of the Forge**

The Temple of the Forge sits on the lower slope of the Temple District, closer to the Marketplace than most of its neighbors. You hear it before you see it: the steady ring of hammers, the low roar of the main hearth, and the occasional sharp hiss of quenching metal.

The building is broad and practical. Dark stone walls, soot-stained around the high vents, a wide open front that can be closed with iron-bound shutters at night. There is no grand idol in the courtyard. Instead a single massive anvil stands under the open sky, its surface scarred by generations of ceremonial and working strikes. Offerings left on it are usually small tools, broken blades, or a pinch of good ore.

Inside, the temple is a working forge first and a place of worship second. Multiple hearths run along the long walls. Smiths and artisans work in the open, some wearing simple iron tokens of the Forge, others simply here because this is where the best heat and the best company are found. The air is hot, dry, and metallic. Sparks drift up into the high rafters and die.

### What the party can get here

**Basic & repair work**  
- Sharpening, mending, re-hafting, simple modifications — priced in silver, done the same day if the queue is not overloaded.  
- Ordinary weapons and armor (no mechanical tier bonus) available off the rack or made to order in a few days.

**Tier 1 gear (the real draw)**  
This is one of the first places in the capital where a party can actually buy proper mechanical equipment. Stock is limited and not always on display.

Typical offerings (examples, adjust as needed):

| Item                      | Type   | Effect                          | Price    |
|---------------------------|--------|---------------------------------|----------|
| Forge-Touched Blade       | Weapon | +1 attack damage                | 200 gold |
| Quench-Hardened Jacket    | Armor  | Armour 1                        | 200 gold |
| Spark-Guard Gauntlets     | Armor  | Start combat with 1 Resist      | 180 gold |
| Temper-Line Short Sword   | Weapon | Inflict Weak on first successful attack each combat | 200 gold |

Higher-tier work exists but is commission-only and measured in weeks, not days. The temple does not keep Tier 2 or 3 pieces sitting on shelves.

### Key faces

- **The Duty Smith** (rotating) — whoever is currently tending the public counter. Practical, soot-streaked, short on small talk.  
- **Master Harran** — older, heavy-shouldered, speaks for the temple when something more than a simple purchase is required. He decides whether a commission is accepted.  
- A handful of independent artisans who rent hearth space and sell their own work under the temple’s roof. Quality varies; the best of them are worth seeking out.

### Atmosphere & rules of the place
- Loud, hot, and honest.  
- Payment is expected in coin or good metal. Favors are sometimes accepted, but only by the senior smiths.  
- Open blasphemy against craftsmanship is the one thing that reliably gets someone thrown out.  
- The temple does not care what you do with the gear once it leaves. It cares that the work itself was done properly.

This is the natural first stop for a party that has coin and needs real equipment.